      {
        "heading": "Does cloud failure mean recording stopped?",
        "accent": "cyan",
        "text": [
          "This fictional training design separates local recording from cloud persistence. The camera is on with no livestream and no recording initially; a local trigger begins recording while the porch is empty; then a person walks through the door while recording continues.",
          "Choose an outcome on the shared topology. All outcomes share camera ready, quiet recording starts, person enters, and the upload request is sent."
        ],
        "bullets": [
          {
            "text": "**Confirmed answer:** a failed cloud interaction does *not* necessarily mean the camera stopped recording."
          },
          {
            "text": "**Timeout branch:** storage and notification delivery are *unknown*, not confirmed absent."
          },
          {
            "text": "**Scope:** scene motion is illustrative; no durations, retry limits, payload identifiers, capacities, or field-of-view measurements are supplied."
          }
        ],
        "contract": {
          "title": "Only inter-component communications",
          "fields": [
            {
              "k": "Camera -> Upload API",
              "v": "HTTPS",
              "g": "upload request"
            },
            {
              "k": "Upload API -> Clip Store",
              "v": "HTTPS",
              "g": "clip write"
            },
            {
              "k": "Upload API -> Resident Phone",
              "v": "HTTPS",
              "g": "resident notification"
            }
          ],
          "note": "The document supplies no API URLs, payload fields, elapsed durations, queue depths, retry limits, storage capacities, identifiers, or field-of-view measurements."
